# MCP Client Configuration
File: mcp/docs/client_config.oot

The server is a live stdio binary. It reads one frame, writes one Content-Length response, and repeats until exit or idle hangup (5 minutes). Set OODACODEX.

## Direct launch

```sh
OODACODEX=/path/to/openOODA/NORTHSTAR.oot ooda mcp
```

## Claude Desktop / Cursor

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "openooda": {
      "command": "ooda",
      "args": ["mcp"],
      "env": { "OODACODEX": "/path/to/openOODA/NORTHSTAR.oot" }
    }
  }
}
```

Merge without destroying other keys:

```sh
ooda mcp-merge ~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json
```

Exit 0 = already present. Exit 1 = written. Exit 2 = error.

## Initialize options

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| protocolVersion | Must be 2024-11-05 |
| clientInfo.name | Recorded on the session |
| clientInfo.version | Recorded on the session |
| tier | minimal, standard (default), audit |

minimal hides tools/resources. audit unlocks ooda://em/metrics.

## Failures

- Immediate exit: OODACODEX missing.
- Idle hangup: no complete frame for 5 minutes. Use `--file` for one-shot.
- -32601: MCP methods only. Not textDocument/*.
- -32602: arguments object does not match inputSchema.
- -32603: missing cap, duplicate id, or cancelled request id.
